s  the case because it would significantly  complement and improve  a monetary  zone that is becoming also  a banking union and clearly down the  road being a fiscal union would help  tremendously so basically what you're  saying you think the germans are going  to come around  you know in europe as as the founders of  europe have observed things happen  through crisis  the crisis that the euro area went  through has been transformational  there has been a renewed determination  to  form that eurozone around the currency  around banking union around better  integration of the fiscal policies i'm  sure that the road ahead is going to  continue to have bumps and hiccups and  difficulties  but there will be  a continued journey towards more  integration  now  um of course an important part of the  german policy was austerity  they've been known to be the champions  of that uh when it comes down to  european economic policy there seems to  have been a shift there with the imf  saying that now we have to focus more on  growth and less on austerity even a year  ago there was sort of an acknowledgement  that there was an error in the system in  calculating how austerity really works  in an economy  are you the symbol of this change at the  imf  first of all i would observe that  austerity in new language in german  means discipline doesn't it  we've always advocated discipline  when the objectives are said they have  to be  respected  what we're also saying is that growth  and  fiscal policies  that results in consolidation  are not mutually exclusive and what  we're saying is that it is the pace of  fiscal consolidation  and the type of measures that are used  to consolidate fiscally that need to be  tailored in order to privilege growth  so this is not an acknowledgment that  the imf got it wrong sometimes with the  austerity issue before that  we're never saying that we are always  right who is ever always right  what we are known for is for  acknowledging when we make 